#: ../../technical/articles/105-profile-facts-registration-recovery-and-session-selection.md:12
msgid ""
"This chunk contains 23 user-profile application modules, totaling 5,252 "
"source lines, 223,485 bytes, and 45,999 measured `o200k_base` proxy "
"tokens. I read the entire assigned code in nine bounded pages, including "
"all explicitly split file ranges. This is static analysis of the supplied"
" snapshot: I did not import or run the application or validate external "
"legal claims. Findings below describe these modules and identify cross-"
"layer questions rather than inferring behavior from names alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/105-profile-facts-registration-recovery-and-session-selection.md:14
msgid "Capabilities and operation"
msgstr "Capacitats i funcionament"

#: ../../technical/articles/105-profile-facts-registration-recovery-and-session-selection.md:16
msgid ""
"The chunk implements much of the profile-management application surface. "
"An operator can inspect and edit schema-backed profile facts, maintain "
"repeatable sections, check filing preconditions, register a profile, "
"rotate its passphrase, enroll or use a recovery code, and select or "
"resume a profile session. Supporting modules provide projections, "
"inventory, record/session access, persistence-facing façades, and "
"presentation hints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/105-profile-facts-registration-recovery-and-session-selection.md:18
msgid ""
"The overview builder constructs sections from the pinned profile schema, "
"includes declared fields even when no fact has been stored, and expands "
"repeatable rows and object namespaces from record facts. For each field "
"it supplies localized label/help and choices, type/value presentation, "
"row identity, and a shared completeness status. Its masking decision "
"prioritizes the schema's `SECRET` sensitivity class; only facts without a"
" schema declaration reach the fallback keyword rules. Indexed row "
"instances retain their base field declaration, so adding `[n]` does not "
"discard secret classification. This is a meaningful data-minimization "
"control at the projection boundary, although safe use still depends on "
"every display path consuming the masked overview rather than raw record "
"values. overview.py (`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/overview.py`) "
"overview.py (`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/overview.py`) "
"overview.py (`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/overview.py`) "
"overview.py (`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/overview.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/105-profile-facts-registration-recovery-and-session-selection.md:20
msgid ""
"Completeness and filing preflight are related but intentionally distinct."
" `ProfilePreflightService` maps required schema facts to model-specific "
"selectors and grounds requirement descriptions in schema and pinned "
"registry metadata. It reports both a readiness result and whether any "
"operation-specific requirements were actually assessed. Therefore, a "
"result marked ready with `per_operation_requirements_assessed` false "
"means this service found no model-specific requirement to assess; it is "
"not evidence that every filing obligation has been checked. preflight.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/preflight.py`) preflight.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/preflight.py`) preflight.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/preflight.py`) preflight.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/preflight.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/105-profile-facts-registration-recovery-and-session-selection.md:22
msgid ""
"Repeatable-row mutations validate the target section and complete row "
"payload against schema, derive stable indexed fact paths, and write "
"through the shared fact mutation mechanism with a baseline comparison. "
"Updates preserve row identity; removal clears the row's facts rather than"
" reusing its index. The calendar-year workforce helper applies this model"
" to plantilla media: it replaces a row for the same year or allocates the"
" next index, and removal clears its three data leaves. This gives callers"
" consistent conflict behavior and stable references to existing rows. "
"section_rows.py (`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/section_rows.py`) "
"section_rows.py (`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/section_rows.py`) "
