"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/profile_pointer.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/105-profile-facts-registration-recovery-and-session-selection.md:34
msgid ""
"`ProfileRecordRepository` is a session-bound current-record gateway, not "
"an unrestricted repository. It distinguishes a session derived from "
"active custody from an explicitly bound session, validates backing "
"liveness and schema generation, and declines access when the session is "
"gone. Its invocation-scoped handoff publishes a record for one CLI "
"operation and consumes it once, reducing accidental plaintext carry-over "
"between commands. The neighboring repository exposes validated committed-"
"capsule summaries and requires a session for an unlocked record view. "
"These rules make the application boundary depend on authenticated, live "
"authority, while concrete storage enforcement and process isolation must "
"be checked in adapters and CLI consumers. profile_record_repository.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/profile_record_repository.py`) "
"profile_record_repository.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/profile_record_repository.py`) "
"profile_record_repository.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/profile_record_repository.py`) "
"profile_record_repository.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/profile_record_repository.py`) "
"profile_repository.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/profile_repository.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/105-profile-facts-registration-recovery-and-session-selection.md:36
msgid ""
"The summary inventory is deliberately non-authenticating: it reports "
"recognized, degraded, or concurrently changed capsule summaries without "
"opening keys, envelopes, recovery material, or a sentinel. It avoids "
"partial inventories and permits per-command reuse only after a successful"
" recognized scan. Projections provide canonical paths, typed fact "
"rendering, schema selection, and taxpayer-scoped values. Their temporal "
"rule is narrower: ordering uses `valid_from`, but `valid_to` is "
"explicitly ignored because no `as_of` date is threaded through this "
"projection API. A closed fact can consequently remain effective in this "
"view. Validation code separately warns about such inert boundaries. "
"Callers needing historical/as-of resolution must use a path that actually"
" accepts a coordinate rather than treating these projections as time-"
"aware. profile_summary.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/profile_summary.py`) "
"profile_summary.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/profile_summary.py`) "
"projections.py (`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/projections.py`) "
"projections.py (`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/projections.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/105-profile-facts-registration-recovery-and-session-selection.md:38
msgid ""
"Smaller modules provide schema migration identity and key records, pinned"
" wizard-key catalogue compilation, safe password-assessment facts, a "
"profile-level repository façade, nonbinding presentation hints, and "
"session-admission orchestration. Admission tries reuse, resume, then "
"credential journey in a fixed order, distinguishes refusal from operator "
"decline, and verifies that the resulting active session is for the exact "
"requested profile. `session_authority.py` composes these access, "
"admission, and lifecycle doors rather than adding an independent "
"authorization model. profile_keys.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/profile_keys.py`) "
"prospective_password.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/prospective_password.py`) "
"session_admission.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/session_admission.py`) "
"session_admission.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/session_admission.py`) "
"session_authority.py "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/user_profile/session_authority.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/105-profile-facts-registration-recovery-and-session-selection.md:40
msgid "Assessment and follow-up"
msgstr "Avaluació i seguiment"

#: ../../technical/articles/105-profile-facts-registration-recovery-and-session-selection.md:42
msgid ""
"The strongest local qualities are centralized schema-aware redaction, "
"version/pinned-schema checks on session-bound record access, explicit "
"one-shot handoff semantics, stable repeatable-row identities, and typed "
"distinctions between failed admission and an operator declining "
"credentials. The modules also expose meaningful result state instead of "
"collapsing unknown or degraded storage into a normal profile summary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/105-profile-facts-registration-recovery-and-session-selection.md:44
msgid ""
"Two review points merit cross-layer verification. First, prove that "
"envelope replacement and record reheading are transactionally recoverable"
" under process interruption, including the recovery-code reset route. "
"Second, trace every user-facing readiness consumer to ensure the separate"
" `per_operation_requirements_assessed` flag is shown or enforced. "
"Separately verify that profile projections with `valid_to` facts are not "
"used for as-of decisions, that refreshed legal-hold evidence reaches "
"destructive preflight, and that callback implementations do not log or "
"persist recovery codes insecurely. The chunk includes no tests or runtime"
" evidence sufficient to settle those questions. Its shared fact mutation "
"port, custody adapters, CLI admission callers, and deletion-evidence "
"capture flow are the most important synthesis dependencies."
msgstr ""

